OL,3,GNEWSAFestival features Yorkshire's
OL,4,ABayeux Tapestry
OL,5,
OL,6,FGuided walks will highlight "hidden
OL,7,Fgems" including Yorkshire's answer to
OL,8,Fthe Bayeux Tapestry.
OL,10,FThe Walking East Yorkshire Festival,
OL,11,Fwhich runs from Saturday until 20
OL,12,FSeptember, is designed to showcase the
OL,13,Fregion's "spectacular landscapes" and
OL,14,F"fascinating heritage", according to
OL,15,FEast Riding of Yorkshire Council.
OL,17,FAmong the events will be a history walk
OL,18,Fand talk about the Battle of Stamford
OL,19,FBridge, fought in 1066, and the
OL,20,FStamford Bridge Tapestry, which was
OL,21,Finspired by the Bayeux Tapestry and
OL,22,Fcompleted in 2021.
OL,23,APub: 11-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
